Hey!

32
00:11:32,818 --> 00:11:34,358
Enough already, Long Nose.

33
00:11:34,698 --> 00:11:36,418
You saw the bottom of the ship, right?

34
00:11:36,598 --> 00:11:38,538
The keel is broken right down the middle.

35
00:11:38,858 --> 00:11:41,578
The outer panels are slipping off and the frame is shot.

36
00:11:41,658 --> 00:11:44,578
With a hull like that, the first wave would rip her apart.

37
00:11:44,578 --> 00:11:49,578
And you think that a complete amateur like you can just grab a hammer and...

38
00:11:49,578 --> 00:11:59,458
You shut your damn mouth!

39
00:11:59,678 --> 00:12:02,138
I don't want to hear another word out of you!

40
00:12:02,138 --> 00:12:06,738
If you so much as breathe, I'll kick your teeth and you hear me!

41
00:12:06,738 --> 00:12:08,218
I don't want to hear you.

42
00:12:08,218 --> 00:12:36,138
Besides, I already knew.

43
00:12:38,218 --> 00:12:42,218
Huh? What did you say?

44
00:12:42,218 --> 00:12:56,218
To be honest, in my heart, I knew it all along.

45
00:12:56,218 --> 00:13:06,218
I knew... I knew the truth! I knew that the Mary was at the end of our life!

46
00:13:08,218 --> 00:13:10,218
I knew it!

47
00:13:30,218 --> 00:13:32,218
Deep down, I...

48
00:13:32,218 --> 00:13:38,218
I... I knew it!

49
00:13:38,218 --> 00:13:46,218
When I heard the assessment, I knew that what I saw on that day back in Skypiea really happened!

50
00:13:46,218 --> 00:13:56,218
At first, I thought I was dreaming that there was no way it could be real.

51
00:13:56,218 --> 00:14:04,218
On one foggy night, in a forest lit with nothing but moonlight, I heard the hammering strikes of a wooden mallet.

52
00:14:04,218 --> 00:14:08,218
It sounded like it was coming from the direction of the ship.

53
00:14:08,218 --> 00:14:12,218
But at the time, there shouldn't have been anybody on board.

54
00:14:12,218 --> 00:14:18,218
I crept closer. It confirmed the sound was indeed coming from the Mary.

55
00:14:18,218 --> 00:14:24,218
The fog was thick, but I'm sure I saw someone there striking away with a wooden mallet.

56
00:14:24,218 --> 00:14:26,218
I... I couldn't figure out who it was.

57
00:14:30,218 --> 00:14:32,218
Whoa! Check it out!

58
00:14:32,218 --> 00:14:36,218
The next day, we awoke to find the ship had been haphazardly repaired.

59
00:14:36,218 --> 00:14:40,218
Even the broken mast was back where it had always been.

60
00:14:40,218 --> 00:14:44,218
But there was something even more peculiar that was bugging me.

61
00:14:44,218 --> 00:14:48,218
Whoever fixed the Mary knew how she used to look.

62
00:14:48,218 --> 00:14:50,218
Despite all the modifications we made to her,

63
00:14:50,218 --> 00:14:54,218
this mysterious person had brought her back to her original shape.

64
00:14:54,218 --> 00:14:56,218
She was still in rough condition,

65
00:14:56,218 --> 00:15:00,218
but she was the same old Mary as she had been before.

66
00:15:00,218 --> 00:15:03,218
The whole situation remained a mystery.

67
00:15:03,218 --> 00:15:06,218
But for some reason, these words lingered in my heart.

68
00:15:06,218 --> 00:15:09,218
I don't know if it's something I actually heard someone say,

69
00:15:09,218 --> 00:15:12,218
or maybe just something I imagined.

70
00:15:14,218 --> 00:15:15,218
Don't worry.

71
00:15:15,218 --> 00:15:21,218
I'll carry everyone for a little bit longer.

72
00:15:23,218 --> 00:15:25,218
I know it sounds ridiculous,

73
00:15:25,218 --> 00:15:29,218
but I... I think it was...

74
00:15:29,218 --> 00:15:32,218
the incarnation of the Mary,

75
00:15:32,218 --> 00:15:34,218
and she spoke to me.

76
00:15:38,218 --> 00:15:42,218
She probably already knew that she was at her limits,

77
00:15:42,218 --> 00:15:46,218
and so she appeared in that form to tell us.

78
00:15:46,218 --> 00:15:49,218
She wanted to reassure us that it'd be alright.

79
00:15:49,218 --> 00:15:53,218
That's what I thought of when I heard her assessment from Galila.

80
00:15:57,218 --> 00:16:00,218
You think I'm completely out of my mind, don't you?

81
00:16:00,218 --> 00:16:02,218
I don't care. You don't have to believe me.

82
00:16:04,218 --> 00:16:06,218
What is it, bro?

83
00:16:06,218 --> 00:16:09,218
Whether I believe it or not,

84
00:16:09,218 --> 00:16:11,218
you said that whoever it was you saw

85
00:16:11,218 --> 00:16:14,218
looked like someone holding a wooden mallet, right?

86
00:16:15,218 --> 00:16:16,218
That's right.

87
00:16:16,218 --> 00:16:18,218
Does it mean something?

88
00:16:19,218 --> 00:16:21,218
Yeah, it sure does.

89
00:16:21,218 --> 00:16:24,218
It means that you saw a Klebautermon.

90
00:16:24,218 --> 00:16:26,218
Kle... Klebautermon what?

91
00:16:27,218 --> 00:16:29,218
A Klebautermon.

92
00:16:29,218 --> 00:16:33,218
It's an old legend that's passed down from sailor to sailor.

93
00:16:33,218 --> 00:16:36,218
It's a very particular type of fairy.

94
00:16:36,218 --> 00:16:38,218
It only dwells on ships treated with great care.

95
00:16:39,218 --> 00:16:41,218
You could say it's the ship's spirit.

96
00:16:43,218 --> 00:16:45,218
It's said that it carries a wooden mallet in its hand

97
00:16:45,218 --> 00:16:47,218
and wears the sailor's raincoat.

98
00:16:48,218 --> 00:16:49,218
At times when the vessel is in danger,

99
00:16:49,218 --> 00:16:52,218
it'll run around the ship and find some way to warn everyone.

100
00:16:53,218 --> 00:16:55,218
I've heard that they help sailors in other ways, too.

101
00:16:56,218 --> 00:16:57,218
But to be honest,

102
00:16:57,218 --> 00:17:00,218
this is the first time I've ever heard someone say outright

103
00:17:00,218 --> 00:17:02,218
that they've seen one.

104
00:17:03,218 --> 00:17:05,218
The more care a ship receives,

105
00:17:05,218 --> 00:17:07,218
the more they grow to appreciate the sailors.

106
00:17:08,218 --> 00:17:10,218
This ship must have been determined

107
00:17:10,218 --> 00:17:12,218
to make sure you made it to the next shore,

108
00:17:12,218 --> 00:17:13,218
no matter what.

109
00:17:14,218 --> 00:17:15,218
Just think about it.

110
00:17:15,218 --> 00:17:18,218
This ship had a caring crew that was so special to her.

111
00:17:19,218 --> 00:17:21,218
She even appeared in human form to reassure them

112
00:17:21,218 --> 00:17:23,218
that everything was gonna be all right.

113
00:17:23,218 --> 00:17:26,218
I betcha she's been very happy.

114
00:17:31,218 --> 00:17:32,218
Mary!

115
00:17:39,218 --> 00:17:40,218
I see.

116
00:17:41,218 --> 00:17:42,218
So, it was you.

117
00:17:43,218 --> 00:17:45,218
You were the one who made those repairs

118
00:17:45,218 --> 00:17:47,218
and spoke to me back then, weren't you?

119
00:17:49,218 --> 00:17:50,218
Mary...

120
00:17:50,218 --> 00:18:03,218
As amazing as that is, I'm still confused.

121
00:18:04,218 --> 00:18:05,218
Tell me,

122
00:18:06,218 --> 00:18:08,218
why would you have a big fight with your crew

123
00:18:08,218 --> 00:18:10,218
when you knew the ship was done for?

124
00:18:13,218 --> 00:18:14,218
It's not that simple.

125
00:18:14,218 --> 00:18:15,218
What that was?

126
00:18:15,218 --> 00:18:17,218
hey

